# Transitioning Features Workflow State

## Current State
The workflow is currently in the **Transitioning Features** state.

## Context Requirements
In this state, the following context is required:
- Completed feature and all its sub-features
- Implementation file with all sub-features marked as [test-passing]
- Test files showing all tests pass
- Next candidate features for implementation

## Available Operations
The following operations are valid in this state:
1. Verify all sub-features are implemented and tests pass
2. Update feature status to [done] in core-mechanics.mdc
3. Finalize documentation in the implementation file
4. Run all tests to ensure no regressions
5. Prepare for selecting the next feature
6. Update active-working-feature-context.mdc
7. Prepare for next feature selection

## Required Context Updates
When transitioning from this state, update:
1. Completed feature status to [done] in core-mechanics.mdc
2. Implementation file with final status and documentation
3. Update active-working-feature-context.mdc to reflect completion
4. Update context-persistence.mdc
5. Document the feature completion in the progress history

## Next State Transitions
From this state, the workflow can transition to:
- **Selecting Feature** - After completing the current feature and preparing to select the next one

## Verification Checklist
Before transitioning to the next state, verify:
- [ ] All sub-features are implemented with passing tests
- [ ] Feature status is updated to [done] in core-mechanics.mdc
- [ ] Implementation file is finalized with appropriate documentation
- [ ] active-working-feature-context.mdc is updated to reflect completion
- [ ] context-persistence.mdc is updated
- [ ] Pre-feature-selection checkpoint has been reviewed for the next feature 